    {
      "id": 59602,
      "name": "j1hopki1",
      "username": "j1hopki1",
      "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/j/58f4c7/{size}.png",
      "created_at": "2013-04-12T03:11:57.000Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Ronway\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/ronway/48/1856_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Ronway:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Your initial thought it correct, as it specifies Projectile damage. Once it becomes fire it is no longer projectile so it no longer gets increased.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>But, since card order matters, doesn't the type change only happen after Micro Targeting's effect? I am only playing devil's advocate here. My post about damage steps says damage type is determined before damage amount cause that's the way I think is should be.</p>",
      "post_number": 4,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T02:35:26.773Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
      "quote_count": 0,
      "incoming_link_count": 0,
      "reads": 0,
      "readers_count": 0,
      "score": 0.0,
      "yours": false,
      "topic_id": 7669,
      "topic_slug": "damage-type-changes",
      "display_username": "j1hopki1",
      "primary_group_name": null,
      "flair_name": null,
      "flair_url": null,
      "flair_bg_color": null,
      "flair_color": null,
      "flair_group_id": null,
      "badges_granted": [],
      "version": 1,
      "can_edit": false,
      "can_delete": false,
      "can_recover": false,
      "can_see_hidden_post": false,
      "can_wiki": false,
      "read": false,
      "user_title": null,
      "bookmarked": false,
      "raw": "[quote=\"Ronway\"]\n\nYour initial thought it correct, as it specifies Projectile damage. Once it becomes fire it is no longer projectile so it no longer gets increased.\n\n[/quote]\n\nBut, since card order matters, doesn&#39;t the type change only happen after Micro Targeting&#39;s effect? I am only playing devil&#39;s advocate here. My post about damage steps says damage type is determined before damage amount cause that&#39;s the way I think is should be.\n",
